# How to cite this repository.  The address below is the only place in this file that names it.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these circuits, the programs or the Lean proof, please cite this repository."
type: software
title: "The Walsh-Hadamard transform with fewer operations"
authors:
  - family-names: Sussman
    given-names: Jacob
repository-code: "https://github.com/jacobalansussman/wht-fewer-operations"
date-released: 2026-10-11
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  Explicit circuits for the Walsh-Hadamard transform that use fewer operations than the textbook's
  N log2 N. When every addition, subtraction and multiplication by a constant costs one, the exact
  transform on N = 8^j points takes at most (5/6) N log2 N + N operations; this count is proved in
  Lean 4, in the circuit model of openai/math. When a multiplication by a constant is free inside an
  addition, there are circuits with 19 operations at 8 points, 52 at 16, and (3/4) N log2 N + N/4 at
  every power of two from 4; these are replayed exactly by programs and are not in Lean. It is a
  better constant, not a better exponent. The circuits were found by computer searches run by AI
  agents (Anthropic's Claude) under the author's direction.
keywords:
  - Walsh-Hadamard transform
  - arithmetic circuits
  - operation count
  - Lean 4
